but positive atmosphere suggests overall good. Egocentric may be a risk.\n\nCandidate D: responsibility, problem solving, concentration, responds to unexpected events adequately (stress resilience maybe). Concerns: moody, loner (crew cooperation). No explicit reliability or decision quality evidence.\n\nCandidate A: leadership, anticipates danger, complex connections, spatial vision (technical competence), but unfriendly, unhealthy (maybe health impact). No explicit reliability or stress resilience.\n\nThus the strongest overall seems between B and C. B has strong technical and stress but communication issues. C has strong reliability and crew atmosphere but communication difficulty and egocentric.\n\nWe need to decide which outweighs. The panel is safety-critical; crew cooperation is essential. B's nasty remarks are serious. C's difficulty communicating ideas may be less severe if overall positive atmosphere. Egocentric may affect decision making but we have evidence of quick correct decisions. Lack of willingness to further education may affect adaptability but maybe less critical.\n\nThus I might shift my vote to Candidate C, aligning with Agent 1, but need to address Agent 2's concerns. I can argue that C's positive crew atmosphere and reliability outweigh the communication difficulty, and that egocentric attitude is mitigated by his concern for others and decision quality. Also note that we have no evidence of C's stress resilience, but his quick correct decisions suggest ability under pressure.\n\nAlternatively, I could stay with B but need to address communication concerns. But Agent 2 already supports B, and we have no new evidence to counter. However we have Agent 1's point that C's positive atmosphere is strong.\n\nGiven the evidence, I think Candidate C is the best overall. So I will change my vote to Candidate C, providing reasoning.\n\nWe need to reference prior discussion: Agent 2's defense of B, Agent 1's shift to C. I will say I now support C because